From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chris <08a487@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:26:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] soc: qcom: msm8994-cpu-boot: Default to the A53 cluster

Without CPU idle states (no PSCI, no SPM power collapse yet) the A57
cores idle in WFI at full clock: on the Nexus 6P the battery's charge
current on a USB data port fell from about 170 mA to about 6 mA with
all eight cores up. Power up the A53 cluster by default; cpus=0xfe on
the command line adds the A57 cluster.

Mark the CPUs it leaves unpowered as not present, so smp_init() does not
wait five seconds for each of them.
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/msm8994-cpu-boot.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/msm8994-cpu-boot.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/msm8994-cpu-boot.c
index 8c53eb63b..edb28c165 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/msm8994-cpu-boot.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/msm8994-cpu-boot.c
@@ -79,9 +79,14 @@
 #define SCM_IO_WRITE		SCM_SMC32(0x05, 0x02, ARM_SMCCC_FAST_CALL)
 #define RELEASE_OFFSET		0x88
 
-static unsigned int cpus = 0xfe;
+/*
+ * The A53 cluster by default: without CPU idle states (no PSCI, and no SPM
+ * power collapse here) the A57 cores idle in WFI at full clock, which costs
+ * about 165 mA, all a USB data port's 500 mA leaves the battery.
+ */
+static unsigned int cpus = 0x0e;
 module_param(cpus, uint, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(cpus, "Mask of CPUs to power up (0x0e: A53 cluster, 0xf0: A57 cluster)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cpus, "Mask of CPUs to power up (0x0e: A53 cluster, 0xfe: both clusters)");
 
 static int msm8994_scm_io_readl(u32 addr, u32 *val)
 {
@@ -323,11 +328,17 @@ static int __init msm8994_cpu_boot_init(void)
 		}
 	}
 	for (cpu = 1; cpu < 8; cpu++) {
-		if (!(cpus & BIT(cpu)) || !cpu_possible(cpu) || cpu_online(cpu))
+		if (!cpu_present(cpu) || cpu_online(cpu))
 			continue;
+		/* smp_init() brings up present CPUs only: skip the unpowered ones */
+		if (!(cpus & BIT(cpu))) {
+			set_cpu_present(cpu, false);
+			continue;
+		}
 		ret = msm8994_unclamp_cpu(cpu);
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("msm8994-cpu-boot: CPU%u power-up failed: %d\n", cpu, ret);
+			set_cpu_present(cpu, false);
 			continue;
 		}
 		msm8994_ldo_config(cpu, cpu < 4 ? LDO_VREF_RET_A53 : LDO_VREF_RET_A57);
